WEBVTT

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:13.540
I was always careful to prioritize
human life above all else,

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:17.540
but that consequentially adopted
the form of abandoning one such life.

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:19.160
I am terribly sorry.

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:22.370
No, it's... Um...

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:23.870
How are they?

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:27.200
Both Miss Minase and Miss Futami
have returned safely.

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:31.830
I just sent someone to get you,
so please return with her once she arrives.

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:37.620
It's okay. Neither you nor Miss Minase
will be reprimanded over this incident.

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:38.950
Excuse me...

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:42.540
What about Imber and Yukiho?

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:45.410
I hate to say it, but...

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:08.040
Kono sora no shita itsu made mo

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:11.910
Sagashi tsuzuketa yume

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:13.450
Hitorikiri...

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:19.120
Doko e minna tabidatsu no?

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:24.660
Kioku no hibi ga toozakaru

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:29.370
Ano koro no egao wa

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:36.160
Mune no naka ima wo sasaeteta

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:46.450
Mugon no yokogao de anata mo watashi mo kitto

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:50.040
Kizu yue no persona wakatte ita yo

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:52.620
Kizu yue no persona wakatte ita yo

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:57.290
Shiawase no tame ni ai no tame dakara to

00:01:57.290 --> 00:02:01.700
Zankoku na tatakai wo kuri kaeshite

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:05.370
Sore de mo namida ga tomaranai

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:09.750
Negau kokoro wa issho

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:16.540
Sorezore no mirai ga yobunda

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:23.120
The
Way
Back

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:24.620
MEDICAL RECORDS
Patient Name: MAMI FUTAMI
Birthday: 5/22/95
Male Female

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:28.660
After that, Tempestas' frame melted away,
only leaving his core behind.

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:32.000
We were successfully able
to retrieve his core,

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.870
but Imber ultimately fell into enemy hands.

00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:38.000
If you combine him
with Nubilum and Hiems,

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:41.700
it would mean that Turiavita now
possesses three of the iDOLs.

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:43.790
Three verses two, eh?

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:48.250
No, Tempestas cannot be used
in actual combat.

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:53.290
I believe it wise to consider it three-to-one
with regards to our battle capabilities.

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:56.500
I can't believe it turned out like this
even after using Vulturius.

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:57.540
Do not fret.

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:59.200
Even in light of that,

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:03.660
Tempestas' appearance more
than outweighs our losses.

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:08.040
Hurry and analyze the data.
Do not put this accomplishment to waste.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:12.250
Old farts are pushy pains in the ass.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:17.250
What's this? Back so soon? I'm impress-

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:19.080
Wait!

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:26.700
Vulturius. Weren't you aware of how
many lives could be lost if you used it?!

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:32.580
But if all went well, we coulda
ended the war in one blow.

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:34.120
That's no excuse!

00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:36.040
Aren't you contradicting yourself?

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:39.000
No matter what the cost,

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:44.830
we must prevent Turiavita from gathering
all five cores and releasing Aulyn.

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:47.700
Weren't you in agreement on that?

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:50.790
At that time, the fifth unit
made its appearance.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:53.080
We were in danger of losing everything.

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:56.120
I merely prevented that from happening.

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:01.290
Turiavita will take advantage of the situation

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:03.910
and try to steal our cores
like a man possessed.

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:08.830
There is no going back now...

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:11.950
Not for either of us.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:18.080
Oops!

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:19.410
Pardon me.

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:21.700
You have my apologies.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:36.200
I'm sorry. I won't make you endure
such humiliation ever again, Nebula...

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:40.160
Well, even after taking that beating,
he still hasn't rejected you.

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:44.000
It means Nebula must have taken
a real liking to you, Forehead.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:44.950
Of course he has!
It means Nebula must have taken
a real liking to you, Forehead.

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:47.830
And besides, none of this
would have happened

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:50.870
if Idiot Ribbon and Yukiho hadn't
come up with that lame idea!

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:53.870
Sheesh! Where the heck
did those two go anyway?

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:58.500
Do you think Iori is still in the dark?

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:02.000
Beats me. But even we know about it...

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:03.200
Yeah...

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:06.290
So, how're the results?

00:05:06.290 --> 00:05:09.160
Right. He hardly responds to anything.

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:12.250
The signals we picked up were all flat.

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:14.160
So he's in hibernation, huh?

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:16.700
With the exception of
his fundamental personality,

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:18.160
all of the surrounding fields
have been wiped clean.

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:21.700
He's probably lost all
of his experience data...

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:26.580
Saved those two in exchange
for his memories, did he?

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:29.700
You truly gave it your best.

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:36.410
Mami! Mami!

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:38.910
Mami, can you hear me?

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:43.660
Huh? Where am I...?

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:44.830
Mami!

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:47.830
Uh...

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:54.540
Big Sis Azusa? It's Big Sis Azusa!

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:56.120
Mami...

00:05:57.540 --> 00:05:58.450
Ma'am?

00:05:58.450 --> 00:05:59.830
It's okay.

00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:02.370
Mami, can you sit up?

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:04.750
Uh, yeah.

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:08.910
Huh?

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:12.580
There is no need for alarm.

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:17.200
You've been asleep... for seven years.

00:06:20.950 --> 00:06:22.330
Seven years...?

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:28.200
This is... me?

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:30.580
Right. That's you now.

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:32.540
Now...

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:36.830
Ami...?

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:40.250
Are you Ami?

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:43.370
That's right.

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:49.120
Welcome back.

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:51.540
Ami?

00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:09.660
You smell just like Ami!

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:15.250
I'm back, Ami.

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:17.540
So?

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:20.620
She's been like this ever since
their touching reunion?

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:22.080
Apparently...

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:26.910
Mami, no one is going to take the food
away, so slow down. Eat nice and slow.

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:29.750
But it's just so super yummy!

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:30.660
Mami...

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:33.200
W-well, this is her first meal in seven years.

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:36.540
Food is one of a person's
three primary needs.

00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:37.870
Even so...

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:42.200
...couldn't she be a little less
messy when she eats?

00:07:42.410 --> 00:07:43.580
Oh, strawberry milk!

00:07:43.950 --> 00:07:47.790
Mami, you need to eat one thing at a time...

00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:51.870
See here! Calm down already!

00:07:52.120 --> 00:07:55.330
Eating like that is bad for the digest-

00:08:04.700 --> 00:08:07.700
That brat! What was she thinking?!

00:08:07.700 --> 00:08:12.580
Now, now. It's not like she did it to be
mean, so why don't you forgive her?

00:08:12.580 --> 00:08:14.160
That isn't the problem!

00:08:14.540 --> 00:08:17.290
Nothing good ever comes out
of babying kids like her.

00:08:17.290 --> 00:08:19.830
Sheesh! I'm going to teach her
some lessons later!

00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:20.910
Yeah, yeah.

00:08:20.910 --> 00:08:24.450
Besides, isn't it Idiot Ribbon's job
to fill this role?

00:08:24.450 --> 00:08:26.450
What happened to the moron?

00:08:28.700 --> 00:08:30.370
I wonder what she's doing...

00:08:32.870 --> 00:08:34.790
It's about time you told me!

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:39.250
Something happened, didn't it?

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:46.080
This feels kinda weird.
It's like I suddenly became an adult.

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:47.450
Are you okay?

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:50.500
Yup! I'm fine! Just fine! Lookie.

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:52.000
Mami!

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:53.120
Are you okay?!

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:55.580
Uh-huh. That hurt...

00:08:58.040 --> 00:09:00.040
Do you remember him? It's Nebula.

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:01.200
'Course I do!

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:06.040
Hey, Nebula! Doing well? Yahoo!

00:09:08.540 --> 00:09:12.040
Say, Ami. Where's Tempestas?

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:18.750
He went bye-bye, didn't he?

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:21.120
How did you know?

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:27.080
Before I woke up,
Tempestas told me, "Bye-bye."

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:29.580
Tempestas did?

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:35.290
That boy, well, he was really nice
and saved my life.

00:09:36.790 --> 00:09:41.450
Back then, I got hurt bad... And so...

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:43.830
"I'm sor...," says.

00:09:43.830 --> 00:09:44.700
Mami?!

00:09:44.830 --> 00:09:48.370
Tempestas says, "I'm sorry."

00:09:48.370 --> 00:09:53.750
Mami... Mami!

00:09:55.120 --> 00:10:00.160
Tempestas disappeared so
he could heal your wounds?

00:10:00.330 --> 00:10:07.950
Yup. He took me somewhere warm
and healed me little by little...

00:10:09.450 --> 00:10:13.160
He's sleeping, isn't he? He looks comfy!

00:10:17.290 --> 00:10:18.000
Mami.

00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:25.160
Aren't these my bonbons?

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:28.540
That's right. I've carried them
around this whole time.

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:33.410
That way I could return them
as soon as I saw you again.

00:10:33.950 --> 00:10:35.250
Ami...

00:10:36.580 --> 00:10:42.370
Hey, Tempestas! Can you see them?
Lookie! They're the same as before.

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:45.120
Hey!

00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:45.660
And that's what happened to Yukiho.

00:11:46.120 --> 00:11:47.410
I see...

00:11:48.450 --> 00:11:49.870
Where's the key?

00:11:50.910 --> 00:11:53.330
Isn't Idiot Ribbon coming back tomorrow?

00:11:53.830 --> 00:11:56.750
Shouldn't you lock
this room up before then?

00:11:58.750 --> 00:12:00.040
You're right...

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:08.250
Why?! Why did you deceive us?

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:15.620
Idiot Ribbon being Idiot Ribbon,
of course she'd fall for it!

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:19.500
Wh-what is this?!

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:19.950
Just
the Two
of Us

00:12:19.870 --> 00:12:26.330
Well, I just so happened to run into
your wife the other day at a sports club.

00:12:26.660 --> 00:12:29.040
A-are you trying to threaten me?

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:38.540
I would never think to threaten you.

00:12:38.620 --> 00:12:42.000
I merely wish to take
a look at some records.

00:12:42.910 --> 00:12:47.540
I want the records of that man
from our headquarters in Geneva.

00:12:47.790 --> 00:12:50.160
Adopting a son-in-law must be difficult.

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:52.910
I'm sleepy!

00:12:53.450 --> 00:12:55.450
I've just got to go home today.

00:12:55.450 --> 00:12:59.250
But the chief said she wants
to run an ignition test tonight.

00:12:59.330 --> 00:13:02.200
What?! At least she could let me
get some laundry done!

00:13:08.580 --> 00:13:10.540
E-excuse me...

00:13:12.580 --> 00:13:13.540
Um...

00:13:14.200 --> 00:13:15.830
G-good morning.

00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:17.830
Upsy-daisy.

00:13:19.580 --> 00:13:22.250
Good morning to you!

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:27.120
What the heck is she doing?

00:13:27.250 --> 00:13:30.120
Beats me.
According to Suzuna and the others,

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:32.830
she's been doing that non-stop
since early this morning.

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:36.000
Good morning!

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:38.000
Hi! Good mornin'.

00:13:38.660 --> 00:13:39.790
So you're back now.

00:13:39.790 --> 00:13:41.870
Right! I got back early this morning.

00:13:41.870 --> 00:13:43.120
That right?

00:13:43.120 --> 00:13:46.200
Uh, are you hurt anywhere?

00:13:46.200 --> 00:13:50.580
I underwent some detailed exams
while I was gone, but they said I'm fine!

00:13:50.870 --> 00:13:53.830
R-really? Isn't that great?

00:13:53.830 --> 00:13:54.370
Yep!

00:13:54.830 --> 00:13:56.160
Y-you know...

00:13:56.160 --> 00:13:57.500
Good morning!

00:13:58.870 --> 00:13:59.870
Haruka?

00:14:02.370 --> 00:14:05.160
Good morning, Ami! And this is...?

00:14:05.870 --> 00:14:06.830
She's Mami.

00:14:06.830 --> 00:14:10.450
I knew it! You really do look just alike!

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:11.910
Mami, this is-

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:13.160
Haruka, right?

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:15.330
I'm amazed you knew!

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:19.040
Yup! After all, Ami said there's
a girl with weird ribbons on-

00:14:20.410 --> 00:14:21.830
I-I'm sorry.

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:23.700
Nuh-uh. It's cool.

00:14:23.700 --> 00:14:27.200
Oh, I know! Putting that aside,
we need to celebrate!

00:14:27.950 --> 00:14:32.830
After all, you've been reunited with Mami!
Same goes for Tempestas.

00:14:33.120 --> 00:14:34.370
Haruka...

00:14:34.750 --> 00:14:39.000
Thank you very much,
but this really isn't the time...

00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:40.660
Why isn't it?

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:44.910
Oh, right! I was in the middle of cleaning.

00:14:45.200 --> 00:14:46.870
I was thinking I'd make this place sparkle

00:14:46.870 --> 00:14:50.410
as a surprise for Imber and Yukiho
when they get back.

00:14:50.870 --> 00:14:51.700
But today is a special day and all.

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:53.580
Haruka, um...
But today is a special day and all.

00:14:53.580 --> 00:14:57.580
All right! Now that that's settled,
I need to get some snacks and juice!

00:14:57.580 --> 00:14:59.290
Just hang tight and wait!

00:14:59.410 --> 00:15:01.080
Haruka, wait...!

00:15:04.950 --> 00:15:06.790
Iori, good morning!

00:15:10.660 --> 00:15:11.620
Haruka...

00:15:13.330 --> 00:15:17.410
For the cockpit, we have taken Nubilum's
spare and are fitting it for Chihaya.

00:15:17.540 --> 00:15:20.120
Once it is installed, we will begin
giving him a new coat of paint.

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:23.080
Also, what should we do
with the cockpit we took out?

00:15:23.410 --> 00:15:26.700
Throw it away... Smash it to pieces.

00:15:27.410 --> 00:15:31.410
You've done well. Mother is most pleased.

00:15:31.870 --> 00:15:33.410
Thank you very much.

00:15:33.870 --> 00:15:36.040
I am sure Chihaya must be happy as well.

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:38.620
She has been reunited
with both you and Imber.

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:40.250
Right.

00:15:40.700 --> 00:15:45.700
In the end, you were acting as a spy
this whole time just to bring this about.

00:15:45.700 --> 00:15:47.330
You're quite the loyal hound.

00:15:47.830 --> 00:15:50.330
You must really love this organization, huh?

00:15:50.330 --> 00:15:51.620
You are mistaken.

00:15:53.750 --> 00:15:56.370
My master is Chihaya.

00:16:04.910 --> 00:16:06.580
Good afternoon.

00:16:07.160 --> 00:16:11.790
This won't get you anywhere.
Mama will be here to save me soon.

00:16:12.120 --> 00:16:13.750
That would be nice.

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:19.500
But you'll learn the truth soon enough,
Miss Bastard-Oh, pardon me.

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:22.450
We had another one of
your kind here, didn't we?

00:16:27.700 --> 00:16:33.330
Sure, the prez said, "Firm up,"
but this is a bit much...

00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:36.250
You've already swum over 3km.

00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:37.660
Really?

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:40.700
That's right! And for starters,
you're just getting better.

00:16:40.700 --> 00:16:41.410
Huh?

00:16:41.410 --> 00:16:43.540
I heard you were sick in bed last week.

00:16:43.540 --> 00:16:47.200
Ah, yeah. But I feel like
I've got ants in my pants...

00:16:48.120 --> 00:16:52.080
Yayoi, you can leave without me.
I'm going to swim a bit more.

00:16:52.870 --> 00:16:56.500
Wait, Haruka! Really!

00:16:58.040 --> 00:16:59.410
This is Yayoi Takatsuki...

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:00.910
...and Haruka Amami's

00:17:00.910 --> 00:17:02.040
"Haruka's Distant"

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:03.250
"Yayoi-style"

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:04.580
"Radio"!

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:05.200
That's Haruka's voice!

00:17:05.200 --> 00:17:07.250
That's Haruka's voice!
I mighta been a mermaid in my past life!

00:17:07.250 --> 00:17:07.830
Haruka...
I mighta been a mermaid in my past life!

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:08.290
Haruka...
I'd say you were more like-

00:17:08.290 --> 00:17:08.580
This is neat!
I'd say you were more like-

00:17:08.580 --> 00:17:09.250
This is neat!
A coelacanth!

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:09.660
What?!

00:17:09.660 --> 00:17:11.750
But it's my dream to be a sea lion!

00:17:11.910 --> 00:17:12.080
Speaking of dreams, this is when
we get our first dream of the year.

00:17:12.080 --> 00:17:13.040
Okay...
Speaking of dreams, this is when
we get our first dream of the year.

00:17:13.040 --> 00:17:14.500
Speaking of dreams, this is when
we get our first dream of the year.

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:16.750
Yayoi, what would you like to see
in your first dream?

00:17:16.750 --> 00:17:18.290
Huh? What?!

00:17:18.290 --> 00:17:20.120
We'll find out after this!

00:17:21.450 --> 00:17:24.790
Let's see, next up is
the postcard segment, right?

00:17:24.790 --> 00:17:26.120
Which one should we go with?

00:17:26.120 --> 00:17:27.250
Hey, Haruka.
Which one should we go with?

00:17:28.000 --> 00:17:30.250
Could we go grab some tea after this?

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:32.790
'Kay! Sure thing.

00:17:32.790 --> 00:17:35.250
Anyway, which postcard should we read?

00:17:36.450 --> 00:17:39.450
CAFÉ
MONSIEUR

00:17:37.040 --> 00:17:39.290
Are you really sure?!

00:17:39.750 --> 00:17:43.250
I never dreamed I'd see the day
I could eat this special parfait!

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:45.910
But my weight!

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:48.950
After all that swimming,
you should be okay.

00:17:48.950 --> 00:17:50.290
Y-you think so?

00:17:50.870 --> 00:17:54.410
You're totally right! Thanks for the treat!

00:17:56.120 --> 00:17:56.620
Yummy!

00:17:56.620 --> 00:17:57.540
Say, Haruka.
Yummy!

00:17:58.950 --> 00:18:00.160
What happened?

00:18:01.120 --> 00:18:01.790
Huh?

00:18:02.870 --> 00:18:08.040
I want you to talk to me about it.
I'll always be there to offer you advice.

00:18:08.410 --> 00:18:11.080
It-it's nothing. Nothing happened.

00:18:11.080 --> 00:18:12.950
You can't hide it from me.

00:18:13.120 --> 00:18:15.000
How many years do you
think we've been friends?

00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:16.500
I mean it!

00:18:17.410 --> 00:18:20.370
It's really... nothing at all.

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:24.950
Jeez, Yayoi! That was so sudden.

00:18:26.120 --> 00:18:27.870
You're that bad off, huh?

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:28.290
Café with
delicious coffee.
Café
Monsieur

00:18:29.450 --> 00:18:30.040
Like I said-

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:31.290
It's fine, really.

00:18:31.290 --> 00:18:33.290
Everyone has something
they don't want to talk about.

00:18:34.700 --> 00:18:38.500
I think I understand you the best, so...

00:18:38.500 --> 00:18:42.000
So if you don't want to tell me,
then that's cool.

00:18:42.200 --> 00:18:44.870
But don't bring your problems to work.

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:46.660
I didn't bring anything to work...

00:18:46.660 --> 00:18:48.620
Then let me tell you something.

00:18:49.540 --> 00:18:52.660
The way you acted today,
it wasn't like you at all.

00:18:53.540 --> 00:18:54.790
It sucked.

00:18:58.330 --> 00:18:59.580
Really...

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:01.620
...nothing happened.

00:19:02.660 --> 00:19:07.370
Dinner is ready, but why don't
we wait for Ribbon to come back?

00:19:07.370 --> 00:19:08.950
Why should we?

00:19:08.950 --> 00:19:12.160
Wouldn't you feel sorry for her
if she had to eat by herself?

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:14.080
Not really.

00:19:15.950 --> 00:19:17.200
I'm back!

00:19:19.200 --> 00:19:20.830
This smells good!

00:19:21.040 --> 00:19:22.950
Welcome home. Your timing is perfect.

00:19:23.080 --> 00:19:26.080
Sweet! I am absolutely starving.

00:19:26.750 --> 00:19:31.160
Ah, no-no! You have to make
enough for Yukiho, too!

00:19:31.790 --> 00:19:34.040
Uh, well...

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:37.330
Yukiho really loves gyoza dumplings,
you know?

00:19:37.620 --> 00:19:39.950
We'll have to leave a bunch for her!

00:19:40.160 --> 00:19:42.660
Let's see, her chopsticks, chopsticks...

00:19:43.910 --> 00:19:49.290
Dear
Yukiho

00:19:44.080 --> 00:19:47.500
Ritsuko, I'm going to put
her birthday card in here,

00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:49.370
so could you have
Yukiho open the drawer?

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:50.700
Sure thing.

00:19:54.370 --> 00:19:56.580
How long are you going
to look the other way?

00:19:57.080 --> 00:20:00.120
Can't you tell? She isn't coming back.

00:20:00.500 --> 00:20:04.080
I-I... That's right! I gotta wash-

00:20:04.080 --> 00:20:05.410
Cut the crap!

00:20:07.450 --> 00:20:12.910
Didn't you see what happened for yourself?
You saw Yukiho betray us.

00:20:12.910 --> 00:20:13.620
Stop it...

00:20:13.700 --> 00:20:15.660
And you saw Imber leave with them!

00:20:15.660 --> 00:20:16.830
Stop it!

00:20:19.620 --> 00:20:20.660
Forehead...

00:20:21.540 --> 00:20:24.000
Then what should I do?

00:20:24.870 --> 00:20:28.910
I figured moping around
wouldn't make things better...

00:20:28.910 --> 00:20:31.040
But is that any excuse to lie to yourself?!

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:31.290
I hate doing it! But what else can I do?!
But is that any excuse to lie to yourself?!

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:34.910
I hate doing it! But what else can I do?!

00:20:34.910 --> 00:20:34.950
I hate doing it! But what else can I do?!
Figure that out for yourself!

00:20:34.950 --> 00:20:36.750
Figure that out for yourself!

00:20:38.450 --> 00:20:39.540
I can't...

00:20:40.040 --> 00:20:41.620
Think for a second about

00:20:41.620 --> 00:20:45.750
how you're putting everyone out
with that transparent act!

00:20:45.750 --> 00:20:46.290
You really-

00:20:46.290 --> 00:20:50.250
Then leave me alone.
You have no idea how I feel!

00:20:50.830 --> 00:20:54.120
Iori, you have Nebula, so there's
no way you could understand.

00:20:54.370 --> 00:20:59.160
Unlike with me, Nebula has been
by your side for a long, long time and-

00:21:02.660 --> 00:21:06.370
Nebula was by my side?
Don't give me that bull!

00:21:06.830 --> 00:21:08.700
Nebula was always far away from me.

00:21:09.040 --> 00:21:11.950
I've been chasing after Nebula
this whole time to get this far!

00:21:12.290 --> 00:21:15.040
I've always been chasing after Nebula!
And I've finally reached this point!

00:21:15.620 --> 00:21:19.000
You're the one who didn't have to do
anything just to be with your Imber!

00:21:19.120 --> 00:21:20.160
Am I wrong?!

00:21:22.120 --> 00:21:23.500
That's not...

00:21:24.910 --> 00:21:26.160
That's not...!

00:21:56.290 --> 00:22:05.200
Toki o wataru seija no you ni

00:22:05.200 --> 00:22:14.200
Donna kodoku ni naite ita no?

00:22:14.200 --> 00:22:23.080
Haruka tooi hoshi o tsunagi

00:22:23.080 --> 00:22:31.620
Ne, omoi o egaku wa, sora o miagete

00:22:33.250 --> 00:22:43.080
Dear boy, itsumo kokoro ni anata o sagaseba

00:22:43.080 --> 00:22:52.040
Ah, dakishimeru hodo ni tsuyoi hikari o hanatsu no

00:22:52.040 --> 00:23:01.000
Mabataku kidou ga futari no mejirushi

00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:12.580
Ima doko de mite ite mo truth kanjitete

00:23:25.950 --> 00:23:40.950
Preview:
The Last Pudding

00:23:26.830 --> 00:23:28.750
I finally get to make an entrance
in the preview!

00:23:28.750 --> 00:23:30.160
I've been waiting forever! Far too long!

00:23:30.160 --> 00:23:32.290
They had to deal with various issues first...

00:23:32.290 --> 00:23:36.160
Naturally, I'll be the heroine starting
next week. I'll have a huge role!

00:23:36.160 --> 00:23:37.870
Uh, well, we'll see you next week!

00:23:37.870 --> 00:23:40.000
What's with that huge grin?!
